({#Bavati, baBUva, aBUt, Bavizyati, Bavitum, BUta#})
.²1 To be, become; {#kaTamevaM BavennAma#}; {#asyAH kimaBavat#} <ls>Māl. 9. 29</ls>
 ‘what has become her fate’, ‘what has become of her’ <ls>U. 3. 27</ls>; {#yadBAvi#}
 {#tadBavatu#} <ls>U. 3</ls> ‘come what may’; so {#duHKito Bavati, hfzwo Bavati#} <ab>&c.</ab>
.²2 To be born or produced; {#yadapatyaM BavedasyAm#} <ls>Ms. 9. 127</ls>; {#BAgyakrameRa#}
 {#hi DanAni Bavanti yAnti#} <ls>Mk. 1. 13</ls>.
.²3 To spring or proceed from, arise; {#kroDAd Bavati saMmohaH#} <ls>Bg. 2. 63</ls>, <ls n="Bg.">14. 17</ls>.
.²4 To happen, take place, occur; {#nAtatAyivaDe dozo hanturBavati kaScana#}
 <ls>Ms. 8. 351</ls>; {#yadi saMSayo Bavet#} <ab>&c.</ab>
.²5 To live, exist; {#aBUdaBUtapUrvaH … rAjA cintAmaRirnAma#} <ls>Vās.</ls>;
 {#aBUnnfpo vibuDasaKaH paraMtapaH#} <ls>Bk. 1. 1</ls>.
.²6 To be alive or living, breathe; {#tvamidAnIM na Bavizyasi#} <ls>Ś. 6</ls>;
 {#AH cArudattahataka, ayaM na Bavasi#} <ls>Mk. 4</ls>; {#dugatman, prahara nanvayaM#}
 {#na Bavasi#} <ls>Māl. 5</ls> (‘thou art a dead man’, thou shalt breathe no longer);
 {#fte'pi tvA na Bavizyanti sarve#} <ls>Bg. 11. 32</ls>.
.²7 To remain or be in any state or condition, fare; {#BavAn sTale kaTaM#}
 {#Bavizyati#} <ls>Pt. 2</ls>.
.²8 To stay, abide; remain; {#asminneva latAgfhe tvamaBavastanmArgadattekzaRaH#} <ls>U. 3. 37</ls>.
.²9 To serve, do; {#idaM pAdodakaM Bavizyati#} <ls>Ś. 1</ls>.
.²10 To be possible (usually with a future tense in this sense); {#Bavati#}
 {#BavAn yAjayizyati#} <ls>Sk.</ls>
.²11 To lead or tend to, conduce to, bring about (with <ab>dat.</ab>); {#vAtAya#}
 {#kapilA vidyut … … pItA Bavati sasyAya durBikzAya sitA Bavet#} <ls>Mbh.</ls>;
 {#suKAya tajjanmadinaM baBUva#} <ls>Ku. 1. 23</ls>; {#saMsmftirBava BavatyaBavAya#}
 <ls>Ki. 18. 27</ls>; {#na tasyA rucaye baBUva#} <ls>R. 6. 44</ls>.
.²12 To be on the side of, assist; {#devA arjunato'Bavan .#}
.²13 To belong or pertain to (often expressed by ‘have’); {#tasya ha SataM#}
 {#jAyA baBUvuH#} <ls>Ait. Br.</ls>; {#tasya tejomayA lokA Bavanti brahmavAdinaH#} <ls>Ms. 6. 39</ls>.
.²14 To be engaged in, be occupied (with <ab>loc.</ab>); {#caraRakzAlane kfzRo brAhmaRAnAM#}
 {#svayaM hyaBUt#} <ls>Mb.</ls>
.²15 To conduct oneself, behave.
.²16 <ab>Ved.</ab> To be prosperous, succeed; {#tato devA aBavan#} <ls>Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 7</ls>;
 <ls>Mb. 12. 228. 1</ls>. Used with a preceding noun or adjective {#BU#} serves
 to form verbs in the sense of ‘becoming what it previously is not’ or
 ‘becoming’ in general; {#SvetIBU#} to become white; {#kfzRIBU#} to become
 black; {#payoDarIBUta#} ‘becoming or serving the purpose of teats’; so
 {#kzapaRIBU#} to be or become a mendicant; {#praRiDIBU#} to act the spy;
 {#ArdrIBU#} to melt; {#BasmIBU#} to be reduced to ashes; {#vizayIBU#}
 to form the subject of; so {#ekamatIBU#}; {#taruRIBU#} <ab>&c.</ab> <ab>&c.</ab> {%Note%}:-- The
 senses of {#BU#} may be variously modified according to the adverbs with
 which it is connected; {%<ab>e. g.</ab>%} {#punarBU#} to marry again; {#AvirBU#}
 to appear, arise, to be evident or clear; see {#Avis#}; {#tiroBU#} to disappear;
 {#prAdurBU#} to arise, be visible, appear; {#agreBU#} to be in front,
 take the lead; {#antarBU#} to be absorbed or included; {#ojasyantarBavantyanye#}
 <ls>K. P. 8</ls>; {#dozABU#} to grow evening or dusk-time; {#anyaTA BU#} to be
 otherwise, be changed; {#na me vacanamanyaTA Bavitumarhati#} <ls>Ś. 4</ls>; {#puro#}
 {#BU#} to come forward; stand forth; {#miTyA BU#} to turn out false; {#vfTA#}
 {#BU#} to become useless <ab>&c.</ab> <ab>&c.</ab>
